M03 follow-up: the gunboat (1100003) reports GUNBOAT_KILLED to the objective
controller (1100004) only when the shore cannon (1100002) kills it. The
controller then fails whichever of 1001/1002/1004 is unfinished. The beach
turrets (M03_Beach_Turret) attack the gunboat continuously, and other Nod
fire can also kill it (M00_Damage_Modifier_DME on the gunboat only protects
it from the star). After such a kill nothing can finish those objectives:
M03_Beach_Scenario_Controller needs the gunboat to send 301,1, and the
controller drops every 302/304 event once 1100003 is gone. The pending
secondaries keep HUD priorities 99/98/97, above the primaries (96..93), so
the default HUD objective pointer stays on the beach or the SAMs for the
rest of the mission.

Give every gunboat death the cannon outcome for the objectives: also send
GUNBOAT_KILLED to 1100004 from the non-cannon branch. The designers'
commented-out 302,2 in that branch shows the same intent. The M03CON018
conversation and the self-addressed cannon-branch event are unchanged. The
normal path, where the gunboat survives or the shore cannon kills it, is
unchanged.

--- a/Mission03.cpp
+++ b/Mission03.cpp
@@ -1246,6 +1246,11 @@
 			Commands->Start_Conversation(id, 100018);
 			Commands->Monitor_Conversation(obj, id);
 
+			// Vita port: give any gunboat death the shore cannon outcome. Otherwise
+			// 1001/1002/1004 stay pending for the rest of the mission and, at HUD
+			// priority 99/98/97, keep the default objective pointer off the primaries.
+			Commands->Send_Custom_Event(obj, Commands->Find_Object (1100004), GUNBOAT_KILLED, 0);
+
 			//Commands->Send_Custom_Event(obj, Commands->Find_Object (1100004), 302, 2);
 		}
 	}
